{"id":"word:hebrew:H3196","type":"word","title":"יַיִן","subtitle":"H3196 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"wine (as fermented); by implication, intoxication","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יַיִן (H3196) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 141 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יַיִן (yayin) means wine (as fermented); by implication, intoxication First listed occurrence: 1Chr 9 29."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יַיִן","transliteration":"yayin","pronunciation":"yah'-yin","strong":"H3196","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3196","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["יָ֑יִן","יַ֖יִן","יָֽיִן","יַ֔יִן","וְ/יַ֥יִן"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",57],["HC/Ncmsa",23],["HTd/Ncmsa",19],["HR/Ncmsa",11],["HRd/Ncmsa",7],["HC/Ncmsc",4],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",4],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",3],["HR/Ncmsc",3],["HC/R/Ncmsc",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"wine (as fermented); by implication, intoxication","usage":"banqueting, wine, wine(-bibber).","full":"H3196. yayin יַ֫יִן 141 noun masculine Psa 75:9 wine (Late Hebrew id. ; Ethiopic : vitis, vinea, vinum ; Arabic ( black ) grapes , see Hom ZMG 1889, 654 ; Sabean וין vineyard , Mordt ZMG 1887, 364 Hom l.c. 659 (both after Glaser); Assyrian inu in vocabularies, but this loan-word from western Shemites, according to Hom Aufsätze 102 ; Jen ZA i, 186 f., ZMG 1890, 705 argues to the contrary) — absolute יַ֫יִן Gen 9:21 84t.; יָ֑יִן 14:18 33t.; construct יַ֫יִן Psa 60:5 ; Song 8:2 ; יֵין Deut 32:18 9 t.; suffix יֵינִי Song 5:1 , etc.; &#8212; wine: a. common drink, for refreshment Gen 14:18 (E?) 27:25 (J), Judg 19:19 ; 2Sam 16:2 ; Amos 5:11 ; 9:14 ; Hosea 14:8 ; Job 1:13 , 18 ; Dan 1:5 +, tonic Prov 31:6 ; article of commerce Ezek 27:18 ; Neh 13:15 ; among supplies in strongholds 2Chr 11:11 ; as making merry 2Sam 13:28 ; Zech 9:15 ; 10:7 ; Est 1:10 ; Eccl 9:7 ; 10:19 ; Psa 104:15 . b. used for rejoicing before ׳י Deut 14:26 , compare Hosea 9:4 ; as drink-offering in prescribed ritual Exod 29:40 ; Lev 23:13 ; Num 15:5 , 7 , 10 ; 28:14 ; among temple stores 1Chr 9:29 ; used also in heathen ceremonial, see Deut 32:33 . c. intoxicating 1Sam 1:14 ; 25:37 ; Gen 9:21 , 24 ; 19:32-33 , 34 , 35 (all J), Isa 5:11 , 22 ; Prov 21:17 ; 23:30-31 , +; || תִּירוֺשׁ Hosea 4:11 ; || שֵׁכָר 1Sam 1:15 ; Micah 2:11 ; Isa 24:9 ; 28:7 (twice in verse); 56:12 12 t.; forbidden to Nazirites Num 6:3 (twice in verse) ( שֵׁכָר וְחֹמֶץ יַיִן חֹמֶץ ), 6:4 ; 6:20 , compare Amos 2:12 ; to Rechabites Jer 35:2 , 5 f.; to mother of Samson Judg 13:4 , 7 , 14 ; to priests entering sanctuary Lev 10:9 (P), Ezek 44:21 ; unfitting for kings Prov 31:4 . d. combinations are : הַטּוֺב יֵין Cant 7:10 = the best wine (read כַּיַּיִן ?) Ges § 133 . 3, R. 1; מַלְכוּת יֵין Est 1:7 royal wine ; יַּיִן אֹצרְוֺת 1Chr 27:27 stores of wine, wine-supply ; הָרֶקַח יַיִן Song 8:2 spiced wine ; הַיַּיִן מִשְׁתֵּה wine-feast Est 5:6 ; 7:2 , 7 , 8 ; יַיִן סֹבְאֵי Prov 23:20 wine-bibbers ; יין נאֹד wine-skin Josh 9:4 , 13 ; 1Sam 16:20 ; יין נֵבֶל id. 1:24 ; 10:3 ; 25:18 ; 2Sam 16:1 ; Jer 13:12 (twice in verse); הַיָּ֑יִן בֵּית Song 2:4 either wine-house , where wine is drunk, feasting-house (De and others), or place of wine = vineyard (Ew and others; compare יַיִן גֶּפֶן Num 6:4 ). e. metaphor of wisdom's drink Prov 9:2 , 5 , compare Isa 55:1 ; of ׳י s wrath Jer 25:15 ( היין כּוֺס ); of confusion sent by תַּרְעֵלָה יַיִן ׳י, wine of reeling Psa 60:5 , compare 75:9 ; of ׳י s awaking for vengeance, like a wine-shouter 78:65 ; of Babylon's fierce power Jer 51:7 ; of love Song 5:1 ; חֲמָסִים יֵין Prov 4:17 ; in simile of one bursting with words Job 32:19 ; of disheartened prophet Jer 23:9 ( עֲבָרוֺיַיִן כְּגֶבֶר ); of lover's mouth Cant 7:10 (see above); love is better than wine Cant 1:2; 4:10.","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to effervesce;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 9 29","keyReferences":["1Chr 9 29","1Chr 12 41","1Chr 27 27","1Sam 1 14","1Sam 1 15","1Sam 1 24","1Sam 10 3","1Sam 16 20"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":141,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 9 29","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַ/יַּ֣יִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 12 41","book":"1Chr","chapter":12,"verse":41,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יַֽיִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 27 27","book":"1Chr","chapter":27,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/יַּ֔יִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 14","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יֵינֵ֖/ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp2fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 15","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יַ֥יִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 24","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַ֔יִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 3","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יָֽיִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 16 20","book":"1Sam","chapter":16,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַ֔יִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 18","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַ֗יִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 37","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":37,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/יַּ֨יִן֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 2 9","book":"2Chr","chapter":2,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יַ֗יִן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 2 14","book":"2Chr","chapter":2,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַ/יַּ֨יִן֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 11 11","book":"2Chr","chapter":11,"verse":11,"e